+## Receipt records (spike branch only; not adopted)
+
+Prototype operators for the receipt spike (docs/reviews/receipt-spike.md),
+Model A. They exist on the spike branch only; no item on `main` uses them.
+They are written here as an engine team would receive them if the product
+owner adopts receipt records as an exception to the engine guardrail.
+
+**Input.** A person-scope supplied fact of type `list of receipts`
+(`receipts`): a list of records, each with a `kind` (one of the item's
+options) and an `amount`, and the optional fields its `record_fields`
+declares, each with its type and either `required` or a `default`. Unstated
+list: unknown. Stated empty list: no receipts. A field a record does not
+state takes its declared default; a field with no default is unknown, and is
+reported on the trace as a missing supplied fact named
+`receipts[<index> <kind>].<field>`.
+
+| Operator | Arguments | Result | Unknown | Rule text that needs it |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `sum_receipts` (P55) | list, condition, value | the sum of the value over the records whose condition is true, with **that receipt** bound to each record in list order; a record whose condition is false is skipped and its value not evaluated | unknown if the list is unknown, or the condition of any record is unknown, or the value of a record whose condition is true is unknown. **No records: 0** | 9 CCR 2503-7 3.752.22.A ("received in the income verification period"); 10 CCR 2506-1 4.402.A.2 (each income converted by how often it is paid); 4.405.E (nonrecurring lump sums, of any source); 9 CCR 2503-5 3.520.786 (exempt by source, for the client, spouse and sponsor alike) |
+| `receipt` (P56) | field name (not evaluated) | that receipt's field, or its declared default | unknown when neither; an error outside `sum_receipts` | as P55 |
+| `received_in` (P57) | month | whether that receipt's `month` is the month, or the record states no month (a receipt that recurs in every month) | unknown if the month is; an error outside `sum_receipts` | 9 CCR 2503-7 3.752.21.I, 9 CCR 2503-5 3.520.785.B.1.a ("counted as income in the month received") |
+
+A derived fact's own rule never sees "that receipt" (as for "that month",
+P54): there are no per-receipt derived items, so a condition used by several
+sums is written in each.
+
